design.custom_css:
/* ---- hero ----------------------------------------------------------------
   Shorter than the engine's photo-hero floor, text across the full measure, the
   three facts as a plate on the open side. pool.css' short-laptop rule (768px
   or wider, 760px tall or shorter) now reads its floor from --zs-hero-floor, so
   that case is answered by setting the variable rather than by out-specifying
   an !important (what the 04/11 pass had to do). The !important below is still
   needed against Elementor's own inline min-height on taller screens, where the
   pool.css rule does not apply.

   Never write a "less than" sign anywhere in this field, comments included:
   the theme passes it through wp_strip_all_tags (functions.php:184), which
   deletes everything from that character to the next "greater than" sign. One
   in this comment silently removed the hero rule and the two after it. */
:root { --zs-hero-floor: 440px; }
html body .e-con.zs-hero.zs-hero--home.zs-v-curve { min-height: clamp(380px, 46vh, 440px) !important; padding-bottom: calc(var(--sec-y) * .34 + 2.2vw); }
html body .zs-hero--home.zs-v-curve .zs-hero__lead { max-width: 52ch; text-wrap: pretty; }
html body .zs-hero--home.zs-v-curve .zs-hero__points .zs-checks li::before { background-color: rgb(255 255 255 / .92); }
html body .zs-hero--home.zs-v-curve .zs-hero__points .zs-checks { color: #fff; font-weight: 700; }
@media (min-width: 992px) {
  html body .e-con.zs-hero--home.zs-v-curve .e-con.zs-hero__text { max-width: none; width: 100%; display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(300px, 380px); column-gap: 72px; row-gap: 0; align-items: center; align-content: center; }
  html body .zs-hero--home.zs-v-curve .zs-hero__text > :not(.zs-hero__points) { grid-column: 1; }
  html body .zs-hero--home.zs-v-curve .zs-hero__text .zs-btns { margin-top: 8px; }
  html body .zs-hero--home.zs-v-curve .zs-hero__points { grid-column: 2; grid-row: 1 / span 3; align-self: center; margin: 0; padding: 26px 30px; background: rgb(14 22 29 / .8); border-top: 4px solid var(--c-primary); border-radius: var(--r-sm); text-shadow: none; }
  html body .zs-hero--home.zs-v-curve .zs-hero__points .zs-checks { display: grid; justify-content: stretch; gap: 18px; font-size: 1.15rem; text-align: start; }
  html body .zs-hero--home.zs-v-curve .zs-hero__points .zs-checks li { padding-inline-start: 38px; }
  html body .zs-hero--home.zs-v-curve .zs-hero__points .zs-checks li::before { top: .12em; width: 26px; height: 26px; background-size: 15px; }
}

/* ---- chapters ------------------------------------------------------------
   Three chapters in a 2-up grid at 390 left the third alone on its own row with
   its two-word title broken across two lines. One per row on a phone. */
@media (max-width: 600px) {
  html body .e-con.zs-chapters .e-con.zs-chapters__row { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  html body .e-con.zs-chapters .e-con.zs-chapter { border-inline-start: 0; }
  html body .zs-chapters .zs-chapter__title .elementor-heading-title { font-size: 1.3rem; }
}

/* ---- services row: the brief's three pages -------------------------------
   "מה אפשר להזמין אצלנו" is the only place the home page names the three service
   pages the brief ordered, and it rendered as a 220px strip of small icons under
   a full-width section title. Given the room that page list earns: a larger
   icon, real card padding, and the link said out loud instead of only implied. */
html body .zs-cards.zs-v-framed .e-con.zs-card__body { padding: 40px 32px 34px; align-items: center; --align-items: center; text-align: center; }
body .zs-cards .zs-card__icon .elementor-icon-wrapper { text-align: center; }
html body .zs-cards.zs-v-framed .zs-card__icon .elementor-icon { width: 64px; height: 64px; font-size: 26px; }
body .zs-cards .zs-card__title .elementor-heading-title { font-size: clamp(1.3rem, 1.1rem + .6vw, 1.6rem); line-height: 1.25; text-align: center; }
body .zs-cards .zs-card__text { max-width: 36ch; }
body .zs-cards .zs-card__text p { text-wrap: pretty; text-align: center; }
@media (min-width: 768px) { body .zs-cards .zs-grid--3 { column-gap: 0; }
  body .zs-cards .zs-grid--3 > .e-con.zs-card + .e-con.zs-card { border-inline-start: 1px solid var(--c-line); } }
/* No "read more" marker is added here on purpose: main.css, standards.css and
   pool.css each remove the arrow from a linked card, so the card title being the
   link is the house pattern and not an oversight. */

/* ---- split:overlap -------------------------------------------------------
   The whole card was centred: a three-line Hebrew title broke ragged, and the
   tick rows, whose markers sit at the inline start of each row, lined up on
   neither edge. Reading matter in RTL starts at one edge; the card now does. */
html body .zs-split.zs-v-overlap .e-con.zs-split__text,
html body .zs-split.zs-v-overlap .zs-split__text :is(.zs-sec__title, .elementor-heading-title, p, .zs-checks, .zs-checks li) { text-align: start; }
html body .zs-split.zs-v-overlap .zs-split__text .zs-checks { display: inline-grid; justify-items: start; }
html body .zs-split.zs-v-overlap .zs-split__text .zs-btns { justify-content: flex-start; }
html body .zs-split.zs-v-overlap .zs-checks li::before { background-color: rgb(255 255 255 / .92); }

/* ---- service-page prose --------------------------------------------------
   The three service pages are the brief's own page list and carry its strongest
   line ("דברים מיוחדים ולא סטנדרטיים"), but they rendered as an unbroken column
   of paragraphs: the argument was in the words and nowhere in the page. The
   opening paragraph now leads and each chapter heading carries the brand rule
   the home page's section titles already use. No copy changed. */
html body .zs-prose > .zs-prose__t:first-child p:first-child { font-size: clamp(1.15rem, 1.02rem + .45vw, 1.38rem); line-height: 1.65; color: var(--c-ink); font-weight: 500; }
html body .zs-prose .zs-prose__h h2.elementor-heading-title::before { content: ''; display: block; width: 44px; height: 4px; border-radius: 4px; background: var(--c-primary); margin-bottom: 14px; }
html body .zs-prose .zs-prose__h { margin-top: 2em; }

/* ---- lead bar ------------------------------------------------------------
   Three 170px fields and a detached submit inside a 900px box: the band's own
   form looked slighter than the identical one in the footer. */
@media (min-width: 992px) {
  html body .e-con.zs-leadbar__box { width: 1080px; max-width: 100%; }
  html body .zs-leadbar__box .zs-form { width: 100%; }
  html body .zs-leadbar__box .zs-form__row { flex: 1 1 auto; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 16px; }
}

/* ---- the band held for the client's video --------------------------------
   The user asked for room on the home page for the promo clip being produced.
   The brief itself does not mention a video (checked in the .docx), so this is
   the ask and not something the brief implies, and nothing on the band claims a
   clip exists or names a date.

   It is a real `overlay` band, composed and finished as it stands: a wide still
   with the process line cut into its lower edge. What is reserved is the shape
   and the position, so the clip takes the same box. Two things are pinned here:

   1. **16/9**, the ratio the finished clip will use, at every width. Left alone
      the band is as tall as the photo and `editorial.css` crops it to 56vh on a
      phone, which is the tall-crop-of-a-landscape-photo fault pool.md warns
      about and the reason this site avoided `overlay` until now.
   2. the same box on a phone, so what is checked at 1440 is what ships at 390.

   The handover JSON is in OPEN-ITEMS.md. When the URL arrives this whole
   section object is replaced by the `video` one at the same index, and these
   three rules simply stop matching. */
html body .e-con.zs-overlay .e-con.zs-overlay__media { height: auto; }
html body .zs-overlay .zs-overlay__media .zs-overlay__img img { aspect-ratio: 16 / 9; height: auto; width: 100%; object-fit: cover; }
@media (max-width: 767px) {
  html body .e-con.zs-overlay .e-con.zs-overlay__media { height: auto !important; }
  html body .zs-overlay .zs-overlay__media .zs-overlay__img img { aspect-ratio: 16 / 9; height: auto !important; }
  /* `editorial.css` pulls the card up 12vh. Against a 56vh crop that leaves a
     photo; against a 16/9 strip on a 375px screen (211px tall) it leaves 110px
     and the band reads as a white card with a sliver of picture behind it.
     Pull it up enough to still cut into the edge, not enough to swallow the
     frame: 179px of the 211 stays visible. */
  html body .e-con.zs-overlay .e-con.zs-overlay__card { margin-top: -32px; }
}

/* ---- the closing lead band: tried, reverted ------------------------------
   A warm orange wash on the footer form band was tried here, to stop the last
   call to action taking the same surface grey as the `facts` section above it.
   It read well and it cost too much: a tinted lead band is the single most
   common piece of furniture in the pool right now, and it took this home from
   36% to 44% like c743850 and 40% like c2910210. The band keeps the kit's
   surface grey. Reported rather than hidden: NOTES, 04/11.

   ---- faq: the site's own corner, and a rule between rows -----------------
   Eight questions on one dark plate, square-cornered and with nothing between
   them, ran together. The theme's `faq:dark` zeroes the radius, which makes
   these rows the only square-cornered boxes on a site whose cards, images and
   buttons are all radius 10. They take the site's own corner now, and a
   hairline per row, which is what the theme's light FAQ already does and what
   the orange marker on the open question implied. */
html body .zs-faq .zs-faq__list .elementor-toggle .elementor-toggle-item { border-top: 1px solid var(--c-line); border-radius: var(--r-sm, 8px); }
html body .zs-faq.zs-v-dark .zs-faq__list .elementor-toggle .elementor-toggle-item { border-top: 1px solid rgb(255 255 255 / .22); border-radius: var(--r-sm, 8px); }

/* ---- one colour for one action -------------------------------------------
   pool.css paints the lead-bar submit with --c-accent, so this band's submit was
   steel blue while the identical submit on the contact page and in the footer
   was the brand orange. */
html body .zs-leadbar__box .zs-form__submit { background: var(--c-primary); color: var(--c-primary-ink); }

/* ---- faq:dark ------------------------------------------------------------
   The white question colour and the white toggle icon that used to stand here
   are now in the theme (pool.css: the questions take --c-dark-ink instead of the
   accent). Only this site's own marker for the open question is left. */
html body .zs-faq.zs-v-dark .zs-faq__list .elementor-toggle .elementor-tab-title.elementor-active { box-shadow: inset 3px 0 0 0 var(--c-primary); }
